{
  "name": "monitor",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/monitor.py): the NILE MONITOR, Varanus niloticus, 1.8 m, the tail 60% of it. A LONG NECK held up and forward; a long NARROW head, flat on top, the snout tapering and rounded, a strong brow over the eye, the ear hole behind the jaw; the FORKED TONGUE, long and dark, darting (its own bone, flicking); a long deep trunk on strong sprawled legs, long toes with big curved claws (`horn`s); a very long STRONG TAIL, deeper than wide (flattened from side to side: a swimmer's), a low keel along its top; small bead scales. Dark olive with PALE YELLOW SPOTS IN CROSSBANDS over the back, yellow chevrons on the neck, yellow bands on the tail, a yellowish belly barred dark. Coats: Nile, water monitor (V. salvator, darker), Komodo dragon (plain grey-brown, x1.6, a yellow tongue).",
